 ## Overview
-An object-order rendering approach for scattered data points (ellipsoidal or spherical kernels) using front-to-back compositing, spatial decomposition, and GPU-based early z-culling for occlusion culling and splat elimination [S1, unofficial]. It differs from its parent [Ellipsoidal Kernel Splatting with Warped Slicing](1290-ellipsoidal-kernel-splatting-with-warped-slicing.md) by replacing the warped slicing planes with a direct screen-aligned slicing pass that outputs vertex attributes for GPU rasterization, enabling efficient occlusion culling via early Z-tests [S1, unofficial].
+An object-order rendering approach for scattered data points (ellipsoidal or spherical kernels) using front-to-back compositing, spatial decomposition, and GPU-based early z-culling for occlusion culling and splat elimination [S1, unofficial]. It differs from its parent [Ellipsoidal Kernel Splatting with Warped Slicing](1290-ellipsoidal-kernel-splatting-with-warped-slicing.md) by replacing warped slicing planes with a direct screen-aligned slicing pass that outputs vertex attributes for GPU rasterization, enabling efficient occlusion culling via early Z-tests [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** A set of $N$ scattered data points, each defined by an ellipsoid (13 floating-point parameters) and a scalar density value $d \in [0, 1]$.
-*   **Output:** A final composited frame-buffer image with normalized density values.
