 ## Background
-This method was introduced in the paper "GPU-Accelerated Volume Splatting With Elliptical RBFs" by the authors of [S1, unofficial]. It extends existing GPU-accelerated image-aligned splatter algorithms to handle unstructured data sets consisting of arbitrarily oriented general ellipsoids of various sizes. The work addresses the challenges of implementing object-order rendering with front-to-back compositing on the GPU without expensive sorting or bucketing operations, by using a spatial decomposition data structure and early Z-culling [S1, unofficial].
